  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "CUBESET returns caption (or \"\") while holding the ordered set, rejects sort_order 1/2 without sort_by as #VALUE!, and rejects sort_order outside 0..=6 as #N/A",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, CUBESET(connection, set_expression, [caption], [sort_order], [sort_by]) displays caption coerced to text (or \"\" when omitted) while holding the tuple set in metadata. Over a workbook data model it orders tuples for sort_order 0 (natural), 1/2 (by sort_by ascending/descending), 3/4 (by caption), and 5/6 (natural), returns #VALUE! when sort_order is 1 or 2 with no sort_by, and returns #N/A when sort_order is outside 0..=6. All 4,319 full-bank CUBESET rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/cube/measured.xlsx (A16-A57, A100-A103) and pivot_cube/oracle.xlsx; 4,319/4,319 full-bank rows match.",
